# HQL — Hyper Query Language

HQL is an experimental typed functional language for querying and computing over
structured knowledge. Querying is one capability: the intended language can
also construct values, evaluate functions, transform data, validate constraints,
and return typed results. Its direction is closer to rust, Kusto, Scala, Haskell, 
or even Lean, rather than to SQL. See [doc/wiki/hql/**](hql)

HyperMarkDown remains the authoring and storage format. Markdown docuemnts are second to it. 
HQL will operate on a typed model of docs, cards, metadata, document structure, namespaces, 
relations, and knowledge graphs. See [[hmd-integration]] and [[design-direction]].

The working bootstrap evaluates integer and Boolean literals and integer
addition. It has no knowledge-source integration yet. See [[first-milestone]]
and the [system declarations](../models/requirements/bootstrap.md).
